2025-05-01 01:58:23 - Thread-602 (execute) - INFO - [Exploration]
Relevant tables / columns and why they matter  
• PACKAGEVERSIONS."System": identifies the package‑manager / ecosystem we have to group by.  
• PACKAGEVERSIONS."Licenses": JSON/ARRAY listing the license(s) each package version declares; has to be flattened and counted.  
• PACKAGEVERSIONS."Name" / "Version": may be handy for sanity checks or later joins but not strictly required for the final aggregation.  
Typical conditions that will be useful  
• "Licenses" IS NOT NULL … ignore packages that report no license information.  
• ARRAY_SIZE("Licenses") > 0 … skip empty arrays.  
• LATERAL FLATTEN(input => "Licenses") … turn the array into a row‑set so every license string can be counted.  

Sample Snowflake SQL exploration path (10 different queries, each limited to 20 rows)

```sql
--Description: 1) Peek at a handful of package records to verify columns of interest.
SELECT "System",
       "Name",
       "Version",
       "Licenses"
FROM   "DEPS_DEV_V1"."DEPS_DEV_V1"."PACKAGEVERSIONS"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 2) List the distinct ecosystems (systems) observed.
SELECT DISTINCT "System"
FROM   "DEPS_DEV_V1"."DEPS_DEV_V1"."PACKAGEVERSIONS"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 3) Show raw license arrays for one randomly chosen ecosystem, here NPM.
SELECT "Name",
       "Version",
       "Licenses"
FROM   "DEPS_DEV_V1"."DEPS_DEV_V1"."PACKAGEVERSIONS"
WHERE  "System" = 'NPM'
  AND  "Licenses" IS NOT NULL
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 4) Flatten the license array to see individual license strings (all systems).
SELECT pv."System",
       l.value::STRING AS "License"
FROM   "DEPS_DEV_V1"."DEPS_DEV_V1"."PACKAGEVERSIONS"  pv,
       LATERAL FLATTEN(input => pv."Licenses") l
WHERE  pv."Licenses" IS NOT NULL
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 5) Count how many times each license string appears inside each ecosystem.
SELECT pv."System",
       l.value::STRING AS "License",
       COUNT(*)        AS "Occurrences"
FROM   "DEPS_DEV_V1"."DEPS_DEV_V1"."PACKAGEVERSIONS"  pv,
       LATERAL FLATTEN(input => pv."Licenses") l
WHERE  pv."Licenses" IS NOT NULL
GROUP  BY pv."System", l.value::STRING
ORDER  BY pv."System", "Occurrences" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 6) How many package *versions* have no license information, per ecosystem?
SELECT "System",
       COUNT(*) AS "No_License_PackageVersions"
FROM   "DEPS_DEV_V1"."DEPS_DEV_V1"."PACKAGEVERSIONS"
WHERE  "Licenses" IS NULL
GROUP  BY "System"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 7) Using a window function to rank licenses by frequency inside each system.
SELECT "System",
       "License",
       "Occurrences",
       RANK() OVER (PARTITION BY "System" ORDER BY "Occurrences" DESC) AS "RankInSystem"
FROM (
      SELECT pv."System",
             l.value::STRING AS "License",
             COUNT(*)        AS "Occurrences"
      FROM   "DEPS_DEV_V1"."DEPS_DEV_V1"."PACKAGEVERSIONS"  pv,
             LATERAL FLATTEN(input => pv."Licenses") l
      WHERE  pv."Licenses" IS NOT NULL
      GROUP  BY pv."System", l.value::STRING
     )
ORDER BY "System", "RankInSystem"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 8) Same as (7) but keep only the top license per ecosystem.
SELECT *
FROM (
      SELECT "System",
             "License",
             "Occurrences",
             ROW_NUMBER() OVER (PARTITION BY "System" ORDER BY "Occurrences" DESC) AS rn
      FROM (
            SELECT pv."System",
                   l.value::STRING AS "License",
                   COUNT(*)        AS "Occurrences"
            FROM   "DEPS_DEV_V1"."DEPS_DEV_V1"."PACKAGEVERSIONS"  pv,
                   LATERAL FLATTEN(input => pv."Licenses") l
            WHERE  pv."Licenses" IS NOT NULL
            GROUP  BY pv."System", l.value::STRING
           )
     )
WHERE  rn = 1
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 9) Check if the most‑frequent license is also the only license for some systems.
SELECT "System",
       COUNT(*) AS "Distinct_Licenses_With_Counts"
FROM (
      SELECT pv."System",
             l.value::STRING AS "License"
      FROM   "DEPS_DEV_V1"."DEPS_DEV_V1"."PACKAGEVERSIONS"  pv,
             LATERAL FLATTEN(input => pv."Licenses") l
      WHERE  pv."Licenses" IS NOT NULL
      GROUP  BY pv."System", l.value::STRING
     )
GROUP  BY "System"
HAVING COUNT(*) = 1
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 10) Final query: most frequently used license and its count per ecosystem.
SELECT *
FROM (
      SELECT pv."System",
             l.value::STRING AS "License",
             COUNT(*)        AS "Occurrences",
             ROW_NUMBER() OVER (PARTITION BY pv."System" ORDER BY COUNT(*) DESC) AS rn
      FROM   "DEPS_DEV_V1"."DEPS_DEV_V1"."PACKAGEVERSIONS"  pv,
             LATERAL FLATTEN(input => pv."Licenses") l
      WHERE  pv."Licenses" IS NOT NULL
      GROUP  BY pv."System", l.value::STRING
     )
WHERE  rn = 1
ORDER  BY "System"
LIMIT 20;
```

Each query is limited to 20 rows and wrapped in double quotes for column names, ready to run in Snowflake.
